  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "After standard Chernoff-Hoeffding and polynomial-time linear programming prerequisites, the target still requires simultaneous typewise payoff guessing, compatible allowed-support constraints, a well-supported approximate Bayesian equilibrium, and purification over independently sampled type strategies with a separate small-type regime. The complete new guessing claim and LP/purification construction are at native1623–1688. This is one H2 constructive pure Bayesian-equilibrium outcome beyond routine equilibrium existence or concentration qualifications; the cited LMM mixed-equilibrium algorithm is not assumed to solve this target.",
  "source_scope_note": "Exact formal Theorem6.1 only: a two-player Bayesian game whose joint type distribution is uniform on the product of equally sized type spaces, normalized payoffs in [0,1], equally sized action spaces, and an existing pure BNE admits a pure epsilon-BNE in the original n^{O((ln n+ln k)/epsilon^2)} time. Complete original Bayesian model, payoff guessing, allowed-support linear program, well-supported inequalities, sampling-to-pure closing and small-type brute-force closing are retained. The source-stated Chernoff-Hoeffding lemma is a named prerequisite, and the previous LMM algorithm is only a comparison. Hidden-clique hardness, general correlated-type hardness and small-support variants are unselected and uncounted. All-page source/output QA completed and exact final actual logs checked. Source-material candidate only; no admission/remote-delivery credit.",
  "source_quirks_note": "The original Bayesian-model definition writes the column strategy codomain as S_row at native1449; the formal theorem separately states equal action-space sizes. The original preliminary description says epsilon/4 at1635, while the complete nested claim states epsilon/8. Every exact source notation, inequality and adjacent proof passage is preserved without correction or mathematical-refereeing conclusion.",
